      "Language": "pol",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The description of the case of 35 years old patient with paroxysmal ventricular fibrillation in a course of Prinzmetal angina pectoris treated unsuccessfully with antiarrhythmic drugs who required implantation of cardioverter/defibrillator. The via-venous cardioverter/defibrillator was implanted (ICD). During 6 months observation ventricular tachycardia and ventricular fibrillation occurred four times and was effectively interrupted by the cardioverter/defibrillator."},
